.TH STOP-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-SERVER.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh \- stop a notification server started by start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./stop-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads
.IR data/notify-server.pid ,
sends SIGTERM, polls for up to 5 s, then sends SIGKILL, and removes the pid
file. A stale pid file is removed. A server started any other way \(em by
hand, or by the
.B org.mu2edaq.notify-server
launchd agent \(em has no pid file and is left running; use
.B launchctl bootout
for the agent, or
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1),
which does both.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/notify-server.pid
Pid file written by
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 in every normal case, including when there was nothing to stop.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&./stop\-mu2edaq\-notify\-server.sh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1),
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
.BR mu2edaq-phone-notification-system .
